  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nDjango Filer is a file management application designed for the Django framework. It streamlines the process of uploading and organizing files and images, providing an efficient solution for file handling within Django applications. The application supports file categorization into folders and ensures proper user permissions for file access.\n\n2) Objectives\n\nThe primary objective of Django Filer is to facilitate seamless file and image management for users, ensuring easy uploads, organization, and permission management. It aims to offer a user-friendly interface for managing digital assets within a Django environment.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Administrators: Oversee file organization and manage user permissions.\n- End Users: General users who upload and organize files and images.\n- Developers: Implement and integrate Django Filer into their Django applications.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- File Uploading: Users can upload files and images, which are then stored in the system under specified folders.\n- File Organization: Files and images can be organized into folders with hierarchical structures, supporting parent-child relationships.\n- User Permissions: User and group permissions can be configured to control access and modifications. Permissions include the ability to read, edit, and add files or folders.\n- Clipboard Management: Supports a clipboard feature, enabling users to temporarily store and manage files before organizing them.\n- Image Details: Stores detailed information about images, such as dimensions, alt text, and captions.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: The system should efficiently handle a growing number of files and images without compromising performance.\n- Security: Ensure secure handling of files and permissions to prevent unauthorized access.\n- Usability: Provide an intuitive interface that allows users to easily perform file management tasks.\n- Performance: Optimize for speed and responsiveness when uploading and organizing files.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0034\nCREATE TABLE `filer_folder` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `parent_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `filer_folder_parent_id_idx` (`parent_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `filer_folder_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`parent_id`) REFERENCES `filer_folder` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `filer_file` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `folder_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `file` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `original_filename` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `size` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `filer_file_folder_id_idx` (`folder_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `filer_file_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`folder_id`) REFERENCES `filer_folder` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `filer_image` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `file_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `width` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `height` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `alt_text` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `caption` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `filer_image_file_ptr_id_uniq` (`file_ptr_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `filer_image_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`file_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `filer_file` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `filer_clipboard` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `filer_clipboard_user_id_uniq` (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `filer_clipboarditem` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `clipboard_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `file_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `action` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `filer_clipboarditem_clipboard_id_idx` (`clipboard_id`),\n  KEY `filer_clipboarditem_file_id_idx` (`file_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `filer_clipboarditem_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`clipboard_id`) REFERENCES `filer_clipboard` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `filer_clipboarditem_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`file_id`) REFERENCES `filer_file` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `filer_folderpermission` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `folder_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `group_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `can_read` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `can_edit` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `can_add` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `filer_folderpermission_folder_id_idx` (`folder_id`),\n  KEY `filer_folderpermission_user_id_idx` (`user_id`),\n  KEY `filer_folderpermission_group_id_idx` (`group_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `filer_folderpermission_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`folder_id`) REFERENCES `filer_folder` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
